      "content": "The Green New Deal's centralized planning and massive government spending will inevitably stifle market competition and economic freedom by concentrating power in the hands of bureaucrats and special interest groups, stifling innovation and entrepreneurship, and creating a culture of dependency on government handouts. This will lead to a loss of incentives for businesses to invest and innovate, as they'll be forced to navigate a complex web of regulations and subsidies. The resulting economic inefficiencies will disproportionately harm small businesses and the most productive sectors of the economy, ultimately undermining the very principles of free market capitalism.",
      "source": "target",
