    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I hear that. But some people argue that the \"centralized\" aspect is actually just necessary large-scale coordination to prevent a climate catastrophe, and that the government role is meant to facilitate a transition rather than destroy markets. Why is that argument being dismissed by most serious economic analysts?",
